  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "In a mixing bowl, beat sweet potatoes, sugar, milk, butter, eggs, salt and vanilla until smooth. Transfer to a greased 2-qt. baking dish. In a small bowl, combine brown sugar, pecans and flour; cut in butter until crumbly. Sprinkle over potato mixture. Bake, uncovered, at 325 degrees F for 45-50 minutes or until golden brown.",
      "group": null
    }
  ],
  "footnotes": [],
  "nutrition": null,
  "importedNotes": [
    {
      "text": "I doubled the topping and layered half sweet potato mixture, half topping, then repeated it. Definitely sweet, definitely good!!!"
    },
    {
      "text": "If doubling the whole recipe, add 5 eggs instead of six."
    },
    {
      "text": "Try mini marshmallows on half of it for the kids."
    }
  ],
